  "All block edges, auction/decision references and expiry dates come from SPRK's 'Summary of restricted radio-frequency band rights' spreadsheet (frekvencu_pieskirumu_kopsavilkums_27feb2026.xlsx, page updated 23.04.2026). Tele2's amounts match its investor spectrum table (Dec 2025).",
  "3.4–3.8 GHz is fragmented: each operator holds two or three 25–50 MHz pieces. Bite's 3600–3650 MHz is Rīga only. SPRK's July-2026 roadmap consolidates the band into contiguous 130 MHz blocks from 1.1.2029, with rights extended to end-2043. A future layout is not drawn because the positions are not yet decided.",
  "Upcoming expiries: 2100 MHz for LMT and Tele2 on 31.12.2027 (SPRK sees no obstacle to extension); LMT 2.3 GHz on 5.12.2027; 2.6 GHz and most 3.6 GHz rights on 31.12.2028; Tele2's 0.8 MHz 900 MHz sliver on 10.9.2028 (SPRK proposes extension to 29.2.2036).",
  "Bite's 28 GHz rights (regional fixed wireless access channels) are not counted as mobile spectrum."
